  "query_preview": "through tonight for all areas given the severity of the\nflooding earlier today. Water level forecasts have been \nincreased for the upper Bay given all of that water that came in\nearlier, with Major flooding and water levels at or above 5 ft \nMLLW for much of Dorchester and into Accomack and interior \nWorcester as Saxis has jumped up rapidly since early afternoon. \n\nHave extended the Coastal Flood Warnings through Fri morning for\nall of the upper rivers/and middle Bay zones, and through Friday\nevening Friday night for the Maryland bayside counties, where \nmajor flooding will likely continue for multiple cycles. Along \nthe Atlantic coast, the warning for Ocean City remains in effect\nbeen extended into tonight to cover and additional high tide \ncycle. \n\nIn addition to elevated water levels, dangerous surf along the \nAtlantic coast will continue to result in significant shoreline\nerosion and localized overwash. High Surf Advisories remain in \neffect along the Atlantic coast through tonight and into Friday.",
